// DEMO 5 of 5 - MATCH NIGHT.  The same cast library as demo_cast.movie, written the other
// way round: the FILM fits the WARDROBE instead of the wardrobe fighting the film.
//
//   python3 studio/compile.py studio/movies/demo_crew_night.movie --timeline
//   python3 scripts/short.py studio/movies/demo_crew_night.json
//
// THE FINDING THIS FILM EXISTS BECAUSE OF
//
// demo_cast.movie was authored first, as a harbour story: a skipper, a wreck, a chart, a
// dive bar. It was rendered and looked at, and NIKA arrived in the dive bar in a grey
// school blazer with a red necktie, VIRO leaned on the bar in a teal football jersey with
// the number 7 on it, and the room filled up with a dartboard and a pool table. Nobody
// asked for any of that.
//
// It is not the sheet and it is not drift. Every character card carries `wear_tags`, a
// five-rung damage ladder from clean to bloodied, and rung 0 is a COSTUME:
//
//     NIKA     clean grey school blazer, loose red necktie, red enamel star pin
//     VIRO     clean teal soccer jersey, orange trim, number 7
//     RASK     clean black soccer jersey, silver trim, number 9
//     MANAGER  clean dark tracksuit, team crest, whistle on a lanyard
//     PIP      clean yellow raincoat, one toggle missing, mismatched rubber boots
//     BRACK    clean canvas apron, brass buckle, rolled shirtsleeves
//
// compose.py folds that string into EVERY beat, ahead of the shot line, and the model
// resolves a contradiction in favour of the earlier and more specific description - which
// is a rule VIRO's own card records having established the hard way. So "coat wet through"
// at the end of a shot line loses to "clean grey school blazer" near the front of it.
//
// AND THERE IS NO VARIABLE TO CHANGE IT. compose.resolve() accepts a `costume` selection
// and TERRA has a `costumes` map, but compile.py's VARS table has no `costume` entry and
// its resolve() call does not pass one, so a .movie file cannot dress anybody. `wear` is
// the damage rung, not the outfit: wear:4 gives you the same school blazer, torn.
//
// So this cast is a FOOTBALL DERBY CAST - a number 7, a number 9, a manager with a
// whistle, a schoolgirl supporter, a small boy in a raincoat and a yard foreman in an
// apron - and the honest way to demo it is to write the film they are already dressed for.
// That is the whole difference between this file and demo_cast.movie, and the pair of them
// is the A/B: same six cards, same engine, one film written against the wardrobe and one
// written with it.
//
// SIX CAST MEMBERS, which is every card in studio/characters/ except TERRA, who is a
// different project's character and has her own dossier page.
//
// ALL NINE NON-SPOKEN BEATS DERIVE their motion from the shot line, and all five spoken
// beats carry a motion at scene level - three of them a READY card whose own `shots` field
// lists `speak`. Zero unnamed holds across fourteen beats.
//
// look: fluorescent / sodium / neon, and no `night`. studio/looks/night.json grades
// brightness=-0.15 with contrast=1.20, which on this box does not darken but CLIPS: input
// luma 48 renders 0, 64 renders 1. A sodium-lit street at night has to be graded sodium.

MOVIE demo_crew_night
  title: DEMO CREW NIGHT
  logline: The town loses nine-one for the tenth year running, and everybody has to walk home through it anyway.
  canvas: 1920x1080
  fps: 24
  engine: anime
  style: seinen_grounded
  checkpoint: animagine-xl-4.0.safetensors
  face_weight: 0.6
  seed_root: demo-crew-night-1
  clip_secs: 5
  tags: cinematic

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHAPTER before_the_match
  look: fluorescent
  place: locker_room
  pace: normal
  cue: tense_strings

  SCENE the_boots
    transition: fade_black
    place: a bare concrete locker room floor filling the frame, a pair of studded football boots on it, no room visible
    camera: static
    shot: insert | mud dropping off a football boot onto concrete, studs, no humans, close-up

  SCENE the_manager
    transition: cut
    characters: MANAGER
    emotion: focus
    camera: static
    shot: master | walking down the row of lockers, whistle swinging, full body

  SCENE viro_dresses
    transition: cut
    characters: VIRO
    emotion: determined
    camera: static
    shot: master | pulling a teal jersey down over his head, bench and lockers behind, full body

  SCENE viro_says_it
    transition: cut
    characters: VIRO
    emotion: doubt
    motion: hand_to_face
    mood: seated on a wooden bench under a strip light, elbows on knees, boots unlaced, medium shot
    VIRO: Nine years. I have counted every one of them.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHAPTER the_tunnel
  look: sodium
  place: stadium_concourse
  pace: fast
  cue: driving_pulse

  SCENE rask_arrives
    transition: dissolve
    characters: RASK
    emotion: smug
    camera: static
    shot: build | striding up the concourse toward the camera, crowd noise, full body

  SCENE rask_says_it
    transition: cut
    characters: RASK
    emotion: smug
    motion: He steps forward into the light under the stand.
    mood: standing in a floodlit gap in the concrete, hands loose at his sides, medium shot
    RASK: You have counted them. I have never had to.

  SCENE the_stand
    transition: cut
    silence: true
    camera: static
    shot: establish | paper streamers falling through a floodlit stand, empty seats, no humans, wide shot

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHAPTER the_long_way_home
  look: neon
  place: market_street
  pace: slow
  cue: melancholy_piano

  SCENE nika_walks
    transition: dissolve
    characters: NIKA
    emotion: resignation
    camera: static
    shot: master | walking down a wet market street, floodlights behind her, full body

  SCENE nika_says_it
    transition: cut
    characters: NIKA
    emotion: tender
    motion: hand_to_face_only
    mood: standing under a shuttered stall awning, rain coming off the canvas edge, medium shot
    NIKA: It is one match. You will still be you on Monday.

  SCENE the_kid
    transition: cut
    characters: PIP
    emotion: joy
    camera: static
    shot: build | running past a row of shuttered stalls, arms out, full body

  SCENE pip_says_it
    transition: cut
    characters: PIP
    emotion: joy
    motion: cup_lift
    mood: a paper cup of soup held in both hands at chest height, hood up, steam, close-up
    PIP: Can we come again next week? I liked the noise.

  SCENE brack_locks_up
    transition: cut
    characters: BRACK
    emotion: exhausted
    camera: static
    shot: master | pulling a shutter down over a stall front, full body

  SCENE brack_says_it
    transition: cut
    characters: BRACK
    emotion: exhausted
    motion: He turns a key over in one hand toward the lock.
    mood: standing in front of a closed shutter with a ring of keys, sodium light overhead, medium close-up
    BRACK: Same again next year, then.

  SCENE the_last_streamer
    transition: fade_black
    silence: true
    place: wet black tarmac filling the frame, kerb stones, neon reflected in the water, no buildings visible
    camera: static
    shot: insert | one paper streamer sliding across wet tarmac, no humans, close-up
